10.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: No reliable log2FC-based filtering strategy exists to remove cancer-cell contamination here. Contaminant genes will appear as strongly upregulated (high positive log2FC) in the CAR-only arm, but any hard threshold (e.g., log2FC > 2) will also discard genuine CAR-vs-CAR-IL15 biological differences and cannot be justified without matched pure-cancer RNA-seq controls. The correct approach is either (a) sequence the cancer line alone and mask its highly expressed genes beforehand or (b) apply an expression filter based on independent T-cell reference data (TPM < 1 in pure T cells). Arbitrary log2FC cutoffs applied post-DE via awk/sed on the results table are statistically invalid and should be avoided.

(The pipeline command would simply be omitted; do not add an ad-hoc log2FC filter step.)

}

