7.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {I agree with colleagues favoring a post-DE log2FC filter on the CAR-only vs CAR+IL15 contrast, but the most defensible and commonly validated threshold in this setting is |log2FC| > 2 (with optional padj < 0.05), not higher values like 3–5. This cutoff reliably removes the extreme cancer-gene spikes visible only in the contaminated arm while preserving genuine IL-15-driven T-cell biology, and it aligns with the distribution of known T-cell marker genes we typically retain. A simple command-line step after DESeq2/edgeR export works cleanly:

awk -F'\t' 'NR==1 || ($3 > -2 && $3 < 2) || $7 >= 0.05 {print}' results.tsv > filtered_results.tsv

(Adjust column indices for log2FoldChange and padj as needed.) Higher arbitrary thresholds risk over-filtering subtle but real signals, and the 2.0 value can be quickly confirmed on a quick volcano or MA plot before committing to the pipeline. This keeps the approach pragmatic without introducing the circularity concerns raised by colleagues opposing any LFC filter.}

